<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="72542" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPOL/590/72542.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="EPOL" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPOL.xml">Education Policy, Organization and Leadership</subject><course id="590" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPOL/590.xml">Advanced Graduate Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>AQO</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Advanced Qual Methods</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 21-Jan-25 - 14-Mar-25.</sectionDateRange><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course is designed to provide students with opportunities to advance their understanding of qualitative methods for educational research. It examines relevant qualitative approaches in education, with a focus on designing a research proposal and developing research methods skills including coding and data analysis.  The course further addresses how to communicate research ideas and findings aligned with research questions and a chosen conceptual lens. An introduction to qualitative methods course is required.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to EDD:Ed Pol Org &amp;Ldshp Onl-UIUC.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-03-14Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ONL">Online</type><start>06:00 PM</start><end>09:00 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><meetingDateRange>Meets 21-Jan-25 - 14-Mar-25.</meetingDateRange><instructors><instructor lastName="Bertrand Jones" firstName="T">B